Package: freex-media-server
Version: [[version]]
Section: video
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Niklas Linz <niklas.linz@mirranet.de>
Depends: ffmpeg, openjdk-21-jre-headless | openjdk-25-jre-headless | java21-runtime-headless | java25-runtime-headless, adduser
Suggests: intel-media-va-driver-non-free, mesa-va-drivers
Homepage: https://github.com/LinzN/freex-media-server
Description: FreeX Media Server - Your Media. Your Server. Your Freedom.
 The FreeX server organises movie and TV show folders into libraries and
 streams them to the browser, with a web interface in the style of the
 well-known media servers:
 continue watching, watch state per user, metadata from TMDB, collections,
 playlists, skip intro, Watch Together and on-the-fly conversion with ffmpeg.
 .
 The web interface listens on port 32500. Configuration is in
 /etc/freex-media-server/config.yml, data in /var/lib/freex-media-server.
